WEBVTT

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.380
We've been getting
a lot of strange customers lately.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.590
Huh... What are they like?

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.720
Even though it's summer,
one girl wears a scarf.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.560
What? That's not strange at all.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.810
It's crazy. I mean,
a scarf in the summer...

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.440
I bet it's a ghost...

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.280
<i>...who passed away in the winter.</i>

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.360
Higashida, it's summer right now.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.710
NORTHERN EXPRESS SPECIAL

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:09.250
So you think I'm lying, Higashida?

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.460
YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE I CAN ASK

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.000
No, I don't think that one bit.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.050
Look, speak of the devil.
Here she comes, Higashida.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.850
That doesn't help me since I can't see...

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.440
Table for one.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.610
In the back is good.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.440
Coffee.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.780
No milk.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.990
See?

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:36.820
<i>Clearly!</i>

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.660
Welcome. Please wait
just a minute for that coffee.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.540
<i>Calm down, Daisuke!</i>

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.500
<i>She may not be a ghost, after all.</i>

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.840
This may be the first time I've seen you.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.800
At this place,
one person brings her baby,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.130
one's got a really high voice,
one doesn't understand the language,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.510
one sees things
that everyone else doesn't...

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.970
There are a lot of weird employees here.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.220
You seem like you've got
your act together the most.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.100
<i>I don't know if that means much
coming from someone like this.</i>

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.980
Um, Miss...

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.440
I beg your pardon,
but are you actually alive?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.280
Coffee!
Thank you for your patience!

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.490
I apologize for this idiot's rudeness!

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.320
<i>I take offense at being called an idiot!</i>

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:23.740
Are you a moron?

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.620
You were way out of line there, Higashida!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.540
Then you can see her, too, Miyakoshi?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.710
What are you talking about?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.220
Higashida, do you think she's a ghost?

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.130
After all, she's...

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.380
No, you're just imagining things.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.510
She interacts normally
with all of us, right?

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.220
You're the only one
saying weird things like that.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.020
You're all weird!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.680
Sorry, but this time,
you're the weirdest of all!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.230
Anyway...

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.400
Why do you claim she's a ghost?

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.280
Actually, I realized it
the first time I saw her.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.910
Her uniform is from my high school.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.620
We go to the same school,
but I've never seen her before, so...

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.130
So you probably just never noticed her.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.130
I would notice somebody like that!

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:16.880
Hey.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.800
This isn't important, but...

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.800
What is it?

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.590
Apparently...

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.300
that girl is the granddaughter
of the old fellow who's a regular customer.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.810
Wha...?

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.770
I see.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.480
So Grandpa still has
lingering regrets in this world.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.730
Do you have any lingering regrets, Miss?

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.530
Regrets?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.150
Not especially.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:44.740
None?

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.200
Why, do you have any lingering regrets?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.370
No. But Miss...

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.870
YOU'RE A GHOST

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.580
<i>You're a ghost.</i>

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.130
If you don't live your
life with a positive attitude...

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.840
YOU WON'T GO TO HEAVEN

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.500
<i>...you won't go to heaven.</i>

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.460
That's no life at all.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.970
It's too late to bring that up now.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.430
<i>I made her cry!</i>

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.060
I apologize, Miss!

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.190
I've always had a weak constitution.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.480
Before the entrance ceremony,
I forgot to wear a scarf,

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.780
got a cold that turned into
pneumonia, and was hospitalized.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:32.700
After that, it just became
a burden to go to school,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.210
so I haven't gone even once.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.380
You're a truant? Go to school!

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.340
After all, I missed my chance
to make friends and if I go now,

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.590
I might get bullied.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:45.130
The students of Higashizaka High
are really busy.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.340
We don't have time to bully anyone.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.600
So come to school!

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.810
Higashizaka? That's the same school.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.140
I'm Miri Yanagiba.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:56.770
MIRI YANAGIBA

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.770
I'm first year, class 5.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.440
The same class as me?

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.770
You can take over, Higashida!

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.990
<i>I missed my chance to make friends.</i>

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.370
RUI NAGATA

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.370
<i>Higashida is troubled
about something again.</i>

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.340
Nagata, can I ask you a favor?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.970
I-If it's anything that I can do...

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.050
I want to introduce you to a girl.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.050
If you met her, it'd help me out.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.610
It's summer vacation!

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.780
Um, everyone gather 'round!

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.620
What's your intent on bringing us into
the forest in the middle of the night, dammit?

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.960
On the way home from work,
I was kidnapped by men in black.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.960
CAUTION:
DON'T GO INTO THE FOREST IN CASUAL CLOTHES

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.420
- Same.
- Same.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.170
I was on my way home
from the convenience store.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:05.920
I was working at the host club
when men in black burst in...

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.760
But I'm glad it's not just me this time.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.510
Why are you here too, Yanagiba?

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.470
Um...

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.770
Yes. Yeah...

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.850
The 20-year-old alliance has abducted
everybody, so no one's at the restaurant.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.770
Shiho, come pick me up.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:22.150
Um...

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.860
Do you work here?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:28.280
Higashi is off today, but is he well?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.700
Higashi?

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.700
Are you a friend of Higashida?

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.160
<i>Right now, the workers are having
a gathering. Wanna come?</i>

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:37.870
...he said.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.830
If you've become that sociable,
then come to school!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.790
Sorry, everybody.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.920
My people were rough with you.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.920
All right! Looks like everybody's here!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.260
Saiki isn't here.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.100
We'll start with a test of courage!

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.310
Saiki isn't here.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.970
Something's gonna appear!

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:58.980
A ghost?

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.270
That's not scary.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.270
A bear!

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.610
Oh, just a bear?

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.230
Scary!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.230
Saiki is waiting alone
at the goal with food!

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:08.690
Yay!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.240
Saiki!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:13.990
We're doing random boy-girl pairs.
Girls pick the names.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.660
SNEAK...

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:18.910
TOUCH!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.840
What?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.300
<i>Good morning, Saiki!!
We're doing a test of courage, but we have
an odd number of people!!
Stay here and prepare the food!!
Watch out for bears!!
-Kouno</i>

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.640
<i>I can't read this.</i>

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.810
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.810
<i>I'll be sold off to some foreign country?</i>

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.270
Help!

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:45.770
Adachi...

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:49.070
If you keep that much distance
between us,

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.860
you're sure to lose sight of me.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.110
Right.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:54.820
Well...

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.410
Over there or there?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.990
It looks like there are a lot of people,

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.830
so maybe if we ask them,
they can tell us where to go.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.000
When there are this many people around,
it cuts the fear factor in half.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.210
My fear factor
is being cranked up right now.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.880
Although it seems like
I scare you most of all, Adachi.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.640
Ever since that day, it feels
like you've been keeping your distance.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.480
It does kind of hurt
to be feared so much.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.110
I guess you really do hate me, huh?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.110
No, that's definitely not true!

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.650
Honest! Just the opposite!

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:32.900
Really?

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.200
I'm glad!

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:45.460
Crying didn't work either, huh?

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.170
Did he leave me behind?

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.640
Um... Are you okay, Adachi?

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:01.140
Adachi?

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:09.980
I ran into Kisaki along the way,
and she told me there really is an animal,

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.690
so I came running back
as fast as I could.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.900
If anything happened
to you, Muranushi...

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:25.290
PANT PANT PANT PANT

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.870
I thought you'd probably appear
in my dreams every night!

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.880
Well, sorry about that.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:31.210
Oh, Kisaki.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.880
What's wrong with Saiki?

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:38.090
He ran off in terror after an animal
devoured the food in the boxes.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.180
He got scratched up, too.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:41.890
Then it was a bear?

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:42.890
Could be.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.770
I'm sure Miyakoshi
could take down a bear.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.150
Oh, definitely.
Although she's dumb.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.230
Young people these days sure are strong.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:59.950
Well, let's go.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.290
Even though you heard there was a bear,

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.750
I'm not seeing any signs
of this being called off.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.210
Hello? Yeah.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.460
Kouno, Adachi wants to talk to you.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.670
Me?

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:17.720
Yeah? Did you get to the goal?

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.880
Yeah, yeah. I know.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.890
I'm leaving right now.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.640
Everybody's waiting by the goal,

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.520
where maybe a bear broke into the food.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.520
Uh-huh...

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.400
Let's just go home.
I really think that's the best call.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.650
We're gonna take a shortcut
to get there first,

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:40.660
but you two have to do
the test of courage to arrive.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.410
After all, everyone else got scared,
so it's only fair, right?

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:45.950
What about you?

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:47.750
Well, good luck!

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:57.210
Fools get colds because
they can't manage their health.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:58.670
What was that?

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:04.350
My mom's probably angry at me.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.100
Won't your parents be
mad at you, Higashida?

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.770
They wouldn't be mad.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:11.440
With those two,
it's basically "anything goes."

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.230
But you've got a good family.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.900
Do you have a fever, too?

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.860
They're somehow creepy
in a mild-mannered way!

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.240
How is that "good"? In what way?

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.700
Well, they're cheerful.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.830
It's called "annoying"!

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:28.750
But still...

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:34.330
My mom is hardly ever home,
and my dad doesn't live with us now.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.840
Oh, really? That must be rough.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.970
My mom is a cooking expert...

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:44.180
Yeah, I know.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.550
...so she's good at making
incredible dishes.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:47.560
Uh-huh.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:51.940
And my dad loves
eating my mom's cooking.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:52.850
Uh-huh.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.690
And he works at a TV station,

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.770
so he also gets to eat a lot
when they're on location.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.030
<i>Sounds like they're happy.</i>

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:00.740
But then...

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:02.900
It's diabetes.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:07.410
LICK LICK LICK LICK

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.370
Mrs. Miyakoshi, even though
cooking is your job,

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.410
you don't think about nutrition
when you make dishes?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.870
You eat too much, idiot!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.420
Well, look, you make such delicious
dishes that I can't help it, Youko!

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.460
It's my fault?

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.040
No, that's not what I'm trying to—

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.130
I see! All right, got it!

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.510
I'm putting you on a diet!

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.390
Don't come back home until your
blood glucose level has dropped!

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:28.300
And I'm gonna raise Hana, too, dumbass!

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:31.980
BLOOD GLUE COZE LEVEL?

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:30.930
So...

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.230
until he gets that down,
he can't live with us.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.230
BLOOD GLUCOSE LEVEL        BLOOD GLUE COZE LEVEL

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:36.480
Higashida?

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.020
Miyakoshi...

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.320
You do have it rough. I had no idea!

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.780
Nice smile, Higashida.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.580
Good. I'm not the only one
with a weird family.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.240
My family's not weird!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:55.960
Is it a ghost, Higashida?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.250
I don't think so.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.250
Then a bear?

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.510
All right, hold on!

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.470
Hey, Miyakoshi!

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.840
What do you think you're doing?

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.850
Well, engage the bear in battle, of course.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.680
There's no way you can win!
Are you really that stupid?

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.730
Don't get cocky, Higashida.

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.690
I'm stronger than you.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.360
Her stupidity stands out
so much that I forgot.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.690
She's damn strong!

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.570
Miyakoshi, don't do anything stupid.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.610
Let's just keep walking
until we get home.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:28.320
Miyakoshi!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:31.910
Come to think of it,

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:36.080
we were a pair for a test of courage
in elementary school, too.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.040
Were we?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.000
Back then, Yuuta...

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.800
<i>I'm kind of scared.</i>

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:46.760
<i>Scared of what?</i>

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.430
<i>Are you stupid? Don't pull on me.</i>

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.470
This brings back memories.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.850
<i>I'm the one who was stupid!</i>

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:57.940
SHAKE SHAKE SHAKE SHAKE

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.190
Sh-Shiho... Forgive me.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.230
Well, is that the way you talk

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.530
after hurting Shiho
so much during childhood?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:06.400
I was really scared that time.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.780
Men are so oblivious.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.990
No matter how much you regret it,
those days aren't coming back.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.240
I know. I'm sorry.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.710
I didn't know anything back then.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.130
Not my own situation or anything else.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.500
The past won't come back,

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:27.510
but I thought maybe
we could start over now...

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:30.720
...as friends.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.310
That's right.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:37.930
After all, we are living
in the present, right?

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:38.690
Shiho...

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:46.030
All right, I'll be your friend,
but as the daughter of a consumer lender,

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:49.530
I'll also collect on the wounds
you inflicted on me as a child.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.070
You're going to pay
for my pain and suffering.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.540
Huh? Shindou, you two are still here?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:58.910
Higashida?

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.210
What happened?

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.460
- U-Um...
- Did you see the bear?

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.550
A bear came out
to get rid of that demon, didn't it?

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:06.960
Calm down, Shindou.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:06.500
DEMON

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:07.710
DEMON

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.210
You're showing your emotions.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.180
Wh-What happened to Miyakoshi?

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:14.180
She's coming.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:15.850
With the bear.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:31.360
The scientific name is procyon lotor.
Carnivora. Fissipedia.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:33.740
The procyonidae family,
common raccoon, I believe.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:36.990
C-C-Car?

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:38.240
Correct.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:41.330
So why are you beat up?

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:43.420
Miyakoshi!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.090
Higashida, you move fast!

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:49.920
I surprised myself, too.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.680
Anyway, my foot just hit something.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.050
- The bear?
- No.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:57.260
PANIC PANIC PANIC PANIC

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:58.720
A raccoon dog!

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.140
That's a common raccoon.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.850
And we thought it was a bear?

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.600
I feel bad.
I really gave it all I had—

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.280
And so...

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.780
This is the culprit
that gobbled up the food.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:12.900
But it's cute, isn't it?

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:13.740
It's not cute.

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.160
Then it wasn't a bear...

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.490
Even you, Muranushi?
Are you disappointed?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.700
No, it's just...

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.750
we went to the trouble of preparing bait.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:27.420
Hey, it's all right now,
so untie me! Okay, Adachi?

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.010
Adachi! We're friends, aren't we?

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:33.550
Is this how weak
our friendship is? Traitor!

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.840
- Let's go home.
- Good idea.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.350
Well, I'm going to call for a pick-up.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.100
Kouno.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:43.230
Bears don't like loud noises, so...

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:45.770
Are you saying I'm staying here?

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:49.520
After all, everyone else got scared,
so it's only fair, right?

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:52.070
Everyone did not get scared!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.650
- I was scared.
- I was scared.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:55.570
What?

00:17:55.910 --> 00:18:00.660
Still, I'm surprised you have
a soft spot for animals, Miyakoshi.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.410
What are you going to do with it?

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.830
Leave it here.
I live in an apartment, after all.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.670
Raccoons can't be raised anywhere.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.500
They're treated as pests
that need to be exterminated.

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.090
They're killed?

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.300
It'll be killed?

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:14.840
I'll keep it!

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:18.430
Unless there's a special case,
they can't be kept as pets.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:21.680
Kamakura can do something to make it
a special case so I can keep it!

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:22.600
Higashida!

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.350
Yes?

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.730
<i>The other day, Higashida...</i>

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.320
Be friends with Yanagiba?

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.990
Sorry. I know how busy you are, Nagata.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.650
No, that's okay.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.860
I've been worried about Yanagiba, too.

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.450
I hope she starts coming to school.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:43.040
Also, my part-time job is a secret.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.160
If everyone found out
and came to the restaurant...

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.880
I'd stop going to school, too.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.250
R-Right...

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:55.510
<i>Higashida has been acting weird
ever since he started working,</i>

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.510
<i>but he's counting on me.</i>

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:59.180
<i>Maybe there is still hope.</i>

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.470
Nagata...

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:05.230
Is she a friend of yours, Daisuke?

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:06.390
Hello!

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.520
S-So you have a girlfriend...

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:14.070
No! I just ran into her before.

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:14.860
For me...

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:16.280
she's the root of all evil!

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:17.610
What's wrong, Higashida?

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:19.610
What was that? What did you
call your superior at work?

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:20.740
SNIFF...

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:24.330
Oh, that's right.
We're on our way to work,

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:27.290
but if it's okay with you,
would you meet Yanagiba now?

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:32.250
Hey, hey, Higashi...

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.710
Hey...

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:37.260
Higashi, play with me.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:36.670
You're heavy!

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:43.390
Look, Yanagiba. It's Nagata,
from the same class at school.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:44.720
That's Yanagiba?

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.850
Play with her.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.140
No way.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:52.230
After all, she seems to be...

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:53.980
an upright citizen.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.320
Yanagiba! I'm an upright citizen, too!

00:19:58.650 --> 00:19:59.650
Um...

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.780
Come to think of it, Miyakoshi,
the girl I met earlier, isn't here.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:07.040
Oh, her cold got worse,
so she went home early.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.500
But I'm sure she'll come
to my house again...

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.250
Every single day,
she comes over and gets all clingy,

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:16.500
not letting go until she goes home.

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:19.510
Even though she knew
she was coming down with a cold,

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:22.550
she wouldn't let go because she said
the hugs were keeping her warm.

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.760
I-It sounds like you have it rough.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:28.600
Oh, yeah. And it was a pain
deciding on a name.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.560
On top of that, there was
all this paperwork to fill out.

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:33.940
B-Birth registration?

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:38.740
<i>I-It seems like she's somehow
gotten the wrong idea.</i>

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:43.620
Um, so Miyakoshi goes to
your house every day,

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:47.660
and you get all clingy with her,
right, Higashida?

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.040
No, no! Not me!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.000
Conbini!

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.250
Convenience store?

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.920
No! Wait a second.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.050
Um, Miyakoshi...

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:59.800
Good luck, Higashi!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.420
I call it Mr. Raccoon, but...

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:02.680
Mr. Raccoon?

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:05.260
The convenience store near your house
is called "Mr. Raccoon"?

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.140
Ah, no!

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:08.600
Higashida, want me to take over?

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:11.100
Conbini and Mr. Raccoon are both names

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:13.560
for the raccoon Higashida keeps as a pet.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.150
Raccoon?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.520
Miyakoshi can't keep it at her place,

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.610
so Higashida took it in
and is taking care of it.

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:23.070
That clears up the misunderstanding,

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:26.030
PHEW

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:26.030
but it doesn't change the fact that,
in the end, you two are close.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.660
I don't even know
why she's so fixated on that thing.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:30.660
Me either.

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:32.620
Probably wants me to fatten it up
so she can eat it.

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:34.170
<i>I doubt it.</i>

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:35.960
Stare.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.300
I neglected Yanagiba!

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:40.630
I-I'm sorry!

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:48.850
You were a little stiff today,
but you have potential, Nagata.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:53.600
You can come here again.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.980
You go to school!

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:36.000
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:29.780
And so, Higashida is raising a raccoon!

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:32.620
My family took care
of explaining the circumstances!

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.200
Next time,
"I Have a Feeling It'll Go Well"!

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:36.000
I HAVE A FEELING IT'LL GO WELL
